ing and implementing a human resource accounting system in China due to its large population and relatively poor population quality.\n\n2. **Question Analysis:**.\n   - The question asks which of the following options can be inferred from the given text.\n   - The options provided are:.\n     A) The necessity of developing human resource accounting in China.\n     B) The wave of high-tech revolution in the world has a great influence.\n     C) The population of our country is large and the quality of the population is relatively poor.\n     D) The competition of human resources has become the key factor of social development.\n\n3. **Inference from the Context:**.\n   - Option A directly states the necessity of developing human resource accounting in China, which is supported by the context.\n   - Option B refers to the wave of high-tech revolution, but the context does not explicitly mention its influence; it only states that it has led to a change in economic competition.\n   - Option C mentions the large population and poor population quality, which is also supported by the context.\n   - Option D states that the competition of human resources has become the key factor of social development, which is also supported by the context.\n\n4. **Conclusion:**.\n   - All the options can be inferred from the given context. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
