messages:   25%|##5       | 152/600 [00:50<01:39,  4.52it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNearly all employees of the factory who have completed their high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate, having easily completed the eight week training course. The high school graduates who haven' t earned the certificate are ones who have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course. Overall, though, most of the factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, if the statements above are true, which one of the following also must be true?\n# Options:\nA) A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\nB) A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the eight week training course.\nC) Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\nD) No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.. I think the correct option is: C\n", "<think>.\nTo solve this logical reasoning problem, let's break down the given information and analyze each option step by step.\n\n**Given Information:**.\n\n1. All employees with a high school diploma have earned their factory safety certificate.\n2. High school graduates who haven't earned the certificate have evening obligations preventing them from taking the course.\n3. Most factory workers have not earned the certificate.\n\n**Question:** Based on the above information, which statement must be true?.\n\n**Step-by-Step Analysis:**.\n\n**Option A:** A large proportion of the factory workers have not graduated from high school.\n- This statement cannot be directly inferred from the given information. The information only tells us about the relationship between high school graduates and those who have earned the certificate, but it does not provide any information about the proportion of workers who have not graduated from high school.\n\n**Option B:** A large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations that have prevented them from taking the course.\n- This statement can be inferred from the given information. Since most high school graduates who haven't earned the certificate have evening obligations, it follows that a large proportion of students with high school diplomas have evening obligations.\n\n**Option C:** Most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\n- This statement can be inferred from the given information. Since all employees with a high school diploma have earned the certificate, and most factory workers have not earned the certificate, it follows that most of the workers who have earned the certificate are high school graduates.\n\n**Option D:** No factory worker without a high school diploma has completed the course and earned the certificate.\n- This statement cannot be directly inferred from the given information. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
