messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nNational pricing: refers to the commodity prices and charging standards set by the government price department and the competent business department in accordance with the authority of the state.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is not subject to national pricing?\n# Options:\nA) A well-known shopping mall has newly imported a batch of high-end cashmere sweaters. for the credibility of the shopping mall, the boss decided to sell the new products at a 30% discount in the first three days of the market.\nB) On the eve of the start of school in the spring of 2005, the education bureau of a certain city issued a notice about the tuition and miscellaneous fees of various schools in the new semester, and asked the school to announce it.\nC) On the eve of the spring festival, in order to safeguard the interests of the general public and stabilize the order of the holiday market, the municipal price bureau approved and announced the maximum prices of some commodities such as poultry eggs, vegetables, and aquatic products.\nD) The charging standards for buses in nanjing are clearly: 1 yuan per ride for ordinary unmanned ticket vending vehicles, 2 yuan per ride for air-conditioned unmanned ticket vending vehicles, and 20% off for passengers with bus cards.. I think the correct option is: D\n', '<think>.\nTo determine which option is not subject to national pricing, we need to analyze each option and see if it falls under the category of national pricing.\n\nOption A: The boss of the well-known shopping mall is selling high-end cashmere sweaters at a 30% discount. This is not a government-set price, but rather a promotional offer made by the mall. Therefore, this option is not subject to national pricing.\n\nOption B: The education bureau of a certain city is issuing a notice about the tuition and miscellaneous fees of various schools in the new semester. This is a government-set price, as it is issued by the competent business department. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing.\n\nOption C: The municipal price bureau is approving and announcing the maximum prices of some commodities such as poultry eggs, vegetables, and aquatic products. This is a government-set price, as it is approved by the competent business department. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing.\n\nOption D: The charging standards for buses in Nanjing are clearly stated, with different prices for ordinary unmanned ticket vending vehicles and air-conditioned unmanned ticket vending vehicles. This is a government-set price, as it is clearly stated and approved by the competent business department. Therefore, this option is subject to national pricing. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
