messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnalogical argument is based on the sameness or similarity of two objects in some attributes, and infers that the two objects are also the same or similar in other attributes. Its logical form is that object A has the attributes of a, b, c and d. Object B has properties of a, b, c. So object B has the property of d.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the followings belongs to analogical argument?\n# Options:\nA) Tao yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, li bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. this shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, comrade bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that comrade bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper. I think the correct option is: D\n', "<think>.\nTo determine which option belongs to an analogical argument, we need to identify the pattern of reasoning used in each option. An analogical argument typically involves comparing two objects based on their similarities in certain attributes and then inferring that they share other attributes. Let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Tao Yuanming does not bow for five buckets of rice, Li Bai does not destroy eyebrows and bend over power. This shows that ambitious people are not proud of high officials and generous salaries.\n- This option compares Tao Yuanming and Li Bai based on their behavior towards wealth and power. It infers that ambitious people (like Tao Yuanming and Li Bai) are not proud of high officials and generous salaries. This is an example of an analogical argument because it draws a conclusion about a broader category (ambitious people) based on the behavior of two specific individuals.\n\nB) Both light and sound have the phenomena of linear propagation, refraction, and reflection, so light, like sound, also has fluctuation.\n- This option compares light and sound based on their common properties (linear propagation, refraction, and reflection). It infers that light also has a property (fluctuation) that sound has. This is an example of an analogical argument because it draws a conclusion about light based on the properties of sound.\n\nC) Compared with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work, Comrade Bethune is extremely responsible for his work and extremely enthusiastic towards his comrades and the people, which shows that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others.\n- This option compares Comrade Bethune with some people who are irresponsible in their work and afraid of heavy work. It infers that Comrade Bethune has a great spirit of being unselfish and dedicated to others. This is an example of an analogical argument because it draws a conclusion about Comrade Bethune based on the behavior of some people who are not like him.\n\nD) Silver and copper are both metals with electrical conductivity, but the resistivity of silver is lower, so silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper.\n- This option compares silver and copper based on their electrical conductivity and resistivity. It infers that silver is more suitable to be a conductive material than copper. This is not an analogical argument because it does not involve comparing two objects based on their similarities in certain attributes and then inferring that they share other attributes. Instead, it is a direct comparison based on specific properties.\n\nBased on the analysis, options A, B, and C all belong to analogical arguments. However, since the question asks for the correct option, we should choose the one that best fits the definition of an analogical argument. Therefore, my final option is: "]] 38%|###7      | 226/600 [01:29<03:08,  1.98it/s] 38%|###7      | 227/600 [01:29<02:26,  2.55it/s]
