ntradicts A. Therefore, C and D cannot be true either. This means only A is true, which satisfies the condition that only one statement is true.\n\n**Option B**: A is true, but no one violated the rules of operation.\n- If A is true, then B must be false because it contradicts A. Therefore, C and D cannot be true either. This means only A is true, which satisfies the condition that only one statement is true.\n\n**Option C**: B is true.\n- If B is true, then A must be false because it contradicts B. Therefore, C and D cannot be true either. This means only B is true, which satisfies the condition that only one statement is true.\n\n**Option D**: C is true.\n- If C is true, then A must be false because it contradicts C. Therefore, B and D cannot be true either. This means only C is true, which satisfies the condition that only one statement is true.\n\nSince all options except D are consistent with the condition that only one statement is true, we need to check if D is consistent with the condition. If D is true, then A, B, and C must be false. However, this would mean that more than one statement is true, which contradicts the condition. Therefore, D cannot be true. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
