messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nIn recent years, community banks in some big cities have been closed frequently. At the same time, a series of new banks, such as unmanned banks, 5G banks and smart banks, keep emerging. Bank branches are bidding farewell to cold glass counters and metal benches. The traditional transaction processing functions of bank branches are weakened, and customized services, product experience, social interaction and other functions are increasingly prominent. As a result, some experts predict that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the followings, if true, best supports the expert's view?\n# Options:\nA) Customers need to enter the door to take the number, wait for the number, to deal with a simple business cost a long time\nB) The introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means has changed people's impression of bank branches\nC) Complex business must be signed face to face at the bank branch, such as account opening, account cancellation, etc., must be handled by myself and manual audit\nD) Online banking, mobile banking and other emerging, bank outlets as the main channel of service is weakening. I think the correct option is: B\n", "<think>.\nTo determine which option best supports the expert's view that traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years, we need to analyze each option and see how it relates to the trend of technological advancements and the changing nature of banking services.\n\nOption A suggests that customers need to spend a lot of time waiting in line at the bank branch. This could be seen as a negative aspect of traditional banking, but it doesn't directly address the technological changes that are making bank branches less necessary.\n\nOption B mentions the introduction of artificial intelligence and other technological means, which is a clear indication of how technology is transforming the banking industry. This supports the idea that traditional bank branches may become less relevant as technology takes over some of their functions.\n\nOption C states that complex business transactions require face-to-face interaction at the bank branch. While this is true, it doesn't necessarily mean that bank branches will disappear. In fact, it could be argued that the need for face-to-face interaction will only increase as more complex transactions become available online.\n\nOption D mentions that online banking and mobile banking are becoming more popular, and bank outlets are becoming less important. This is consistent with the trend of technological advancements and the changing nature of banking services, but it doesn't directly address the question of whether traditional bank branches will disappear within 20 years. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
