ence teaches us the opposite of what Lance concludes**.\n   - This option suggests that Frank is showing that experience teaches us the opposite of what Lance concludes.\n   - Frank is not directly arguing that experience teaches us the opposite; he is using Lance's conclusion to draw a different conclusion.\n\n5. **Option C: Showing that Lance's conclusion involves him in a contradiction**.\n   - This option suggests that Frank is showing that Lance's conclusion involves him in a contradiction.\n   - Frank is not directly showing a contradiction; he is using Lance's conclusion to draw a different conclusion.\n\n6. **Option D: Showing that it has no implications for any real cases**.\n   - This option suggests that Frank is showing that Lance's conclusion has no implications for any real cases.\n   - Frank is not directly showing that Lance's conclusion has no implications; he is using Lance's conclusion to draw a different conclusion.\n\n7. **Conclusion:**.\n   - Based on the analysis, none of the options directly describe Frank's argument as accurately as the question asks. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
