artially correct but not entirely accurate based on the given context.\n\nD) Nano usually refers to structures with very tiny dimensions.\n- The context explicitly states that "Nanostructure usually refers to a microstructure with a size below 100 nanometers." This directly supports the claim that nano usually refers to structures with very tiny dimensions. Therefore, option D is correct.\n\nBased on the analysis, the correct statements are A, B, and D. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
