 waste into a new resource.\n\nB) This option describes the use of municipal solid waste incineration for power generation. While this is a form of waste treatment, it is not a form of recycling. Incineration does not create a new resource; instead, it converts waste into energy.\n\nC) This option describes the classification of garbage into recyclable and non-recyclable materials. It then describes how these materials are handled. This is a form of recycling because it involves sorting waste into different categories and then processing them into new resources.\n\nD) This option describes a new way of garbage disposal that involves separating organic matter and inorganic matter. While this is a form of waste treatment, it is not a form of recycling. The goal is to separate waste into different categories, but it does not involve transforming waste into a new resource. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
