on.\n   - This option suggests that if the election is fair, Popov won't win, but since he won, the election must be unfair. This is similar to the given context where if Juan went to the party, it's unlikely Maria enjoyed it, but since Maria did enjoy it, it's unlikely Juan was at the party.\n\n4. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
