gain.\nThis option suggests that regular exercise can prevent weight gain, which would support the argument that replacing an unhealthy activity with a healthy one can help with quitting smoking.\n\nB) Each group in the study included four hundred randomly selected participants.\nThis option provides information about the sample size of the study, but it does not directly support or refute the argument.\n\nC) Nonsmokers accustomed to regular exercise do not gain weight when they stop exercising.\nThis option suggests that nonsmokers accustomed to regular exercise do not gain weight when they stop exercising, which would support the argument that replacing an unhealthy activity with a healthy one can help with quitting smoking.\n\nD) Aerobic exercise can stimulate the brain's production of endorphins, which reduce tension. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
