ime. It does not directly challenge the conclusion that violent crime is out of control.\n\nB) **National data show that violent crime is out of control everywhere, not just in the author's city.**.\n- This option provides external evidence that supports the conclusion that violent crime is out of control. It does not cast serious doubt on the conclusion.\n\nC) **Police records show that people experience more violent crimes in their own neighborhoods than they do outside their neighborhoods.**.\n- This option suggests that the increase in violent crime stories is due to a higher incidence of crime in specific areas, rather than an overall increase in crime. It challenges the conclusion that violent crime is out of control by pointing to localized issues.\n\nD) **News magazines play a more important role today in informing the public about crime than they did in the old days.**.\n- This option suggests that the increase in violent crime stories is due to the role of news magazines, not necessarily an increase in actual crime. It does not directly challenge the conclusion that violent crime is out of control. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
