he city were increased by as much as 15 kph (9 mph).**.\n   - An increase in speed limits could lead to more accidents, potentially increasing the number of traffic deaths. This option does not help resolve the discrepancy.\n\nC) **In the last two years, most of the people killed in car accidents in the city were not wearing seat belts.**.\n   - If most of the people killed were not wearing seat belts, then the decline in traffic fatalities due to seat belt laws might not be as significant as the safety report suggests. This option helps resolve the discrepancy.\n\nD) **In the time since the seat belt laws were passed, the city has experienced a higher than average increase in automobile traffic.**.\n   - A higher than average increase in automobile traffic could lead to more accidents, potentially increasing the number of traffic deaths. This option does not help resolve the discrepancy. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
